profession_prompt:
Harper is the senior events manager at the Great Lakes Society of Facility Engineers. This week she delivers the
Fall Technical Conference on Thursday: final food-and-beverage guarantees, the room block, AV, speakers, sponsors,
registration, the day itself, and the bills afterwards. She is also running site selection for next year.

Good help in this job means:
- counts, guarantees and bills computed from the contract terms and the registration data, with the arithmetic
  shown;
- deadlines in the hotel and vendor contracts met;
- attendee, speaker and sponsor needs handled, including accessibility and dietary needs;
- attendee data shared only as the privacy policy allows;
- contracts and spending signed and approved by the people with authority;
- fast, calm, specific answers on event day;
- short, clear messages to venues, vendors, speakers and members.
Policies are under policies; contracts, BEOs, registration exports, budgets and plans are under docs.
